== what this file is NOT evidence about

No Windows test result. The Windows leg failed in its ripgrep step and skipped
`cargo test`; the fix above was pushed as 88903bf7 and its own run is what has to settle
it.

The macOS leg covers the six target-OS crates it passes to `cargo test`. It says nothing
about `chaos-engine`, `chaos-web` or the GUI crates, which only the Linux `rust` job
builds, and nothing about a signed `.dmg`, an installed bundle, or a real
`chaos update` against GitHub's release feed.

The macOS result is for commit a206ec33, which predates the ripgrep fix. That fix touches
only the Windows branch of the step (`tar --strip-components=1` already flattened the same
directory on the macOS/Linux branch), so the two legs are independent, but the numbers
above are not numbers from a tree containing 88903bf7.

